.TH "NAME CHANGE COMMAND"
The name change command is used to change your "tycoon" name,
the name of a chain in which you are a major holder,
or the name (logname) of the person who is allowed to speak for you.
.s3
To change your tycoon name the command is:
.EX "name t [ new-name ]"
You may change your name to any character
string of 23 or fewer characters, but remember that you'll have to
type this name fairly often and you'll need to put quotes around it
if it contains blanks...
.s3
To change the name of a chain the command is:
.EX "name c [ old-name [ new-name ] ]"
If you are the major holder (or one of the major holders) in the chain
you may change chain names to any character
string of 23 or fewer characters that begins with the same initial
letter as the old chain name.
Only the initial letter need be specified fo rthe "old-name".
.s3
To change the "user" or "login" name of the person who represents
you use the command:
.EX "name u [ log-name ]"
This command allows you to give someone your "proxy".
If you're going to be away from the office but want someone to take care of
your interests without needing to know your password, etc. this is the
command to use.
BEWARE: Unpredictable behaviour is likely if two tycoons have the same "tycoon"
name and the same "user" name.
.s3
If you don't specify the arguments shown here in brackets
on the command line ff will prompt you for them.
